From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: simplefb: describe internal panel transport

KWin/PowerDevil associates internal backlights only with internal outputs.
The Unknown simpledrm connector on SM-T531 leaves its working LP8556 PWM
backlight unmatched and enables software brightness, adding an expensive
full-screen rendering pass on Adreno 305.

Describe the verified LVDS transport behind the board's TC358764 bridge.
Use a local binding extension until native DRM panel topology is complete;
this does not claim an exact LCD module or initialize any bridge/MDP block.
Unknown remains the default for existing firmware framebuffers.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
index 0086cfffd..ad2df13b8 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
@@ -122,6 +122,14 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description: Backlight associated with the firmware framebuffer
 
+  connector-type:
+    description: |
+      Transport to the internal panel driven by firmware. This allows
+      userspace to associate an internal backlight with the output while
+      native modesetting is unavailable. It does not enable display hardware
+      or change the firmware mode. Omit when the transport is unknown.
+    enum: [lvds, edp, dsi, dpi]
+
   display:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description: Primary display hardware node
